# The steps of the parallel set that write the same place, so the gate runner
# (factory/core/verify.sh) never runs them at the same time: a line per set,
# space-separated (factory/core/lib/steps.sh, FACTORY_NO_OVERLAP). None here, so
# typecheck, lint, arch, deviation and test all run at once. What each writes,
# past a temp folder of its own:
#   typecheck  tsc --noEmit, through tsconfig.json's incremental, writes
#              tsconfig.tsbuildinfo, which no other step reads or writes
#   lint       ESLint runs with no --cache, so it writes no .eslintcache
#   arch       dependency-cruiser runs with no --cache; ESLint's config API
#              writes nothing
#   deviation  the Core's (deviation.sh): it reads git and writes nothing else
#   test       Vitest keeps its results cache under node_modules/.vite/vitest,
#              which no other step reads; the project's tests keep their files
#              in the system's temp folder
# None writes .next/ (prepare's next typegen does, before them; smoke's build
# after them) or node_modules/ past Vitest's own cache. A step that comes to
# write where another reads or writes gets a line here naming both.
